\f0\fs24 \cf0 De Sup protein\
Protect against radiation - prevents the radiation from snapping apart.\
If the D-sup protein could be transferred to human DNA.\
\
\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Unique DNA-associating protein that contributes to the exceptional tolerance to harsh environmental stresses (PubMed:{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.uniprot.org/citations/27649274"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \ul \ulc0 27649274}}). Suppresses X-ray-induced DNA damage including single-strand breaks (SSBs) as well as more hazardous double-strand breaks (DSBs) and improves radiotolerance (PubMed:{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.uniprot.org/citations/27649274"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \ul \ulc0 27649274}}). Shields also DNA against reactive oxygene species (ROS) (PubMed:{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.uniprot.org/citations/27649274"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \ul \ulc0 27649274}}).1 Publication\
